        <Options>
            <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="false" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
                <Vermiculite code="1">
                    <English>Unknown</English>
                    <French>Inconnu</French>
                </Vermiculite>
            </Main>
            <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:



-	Some windows

-	Exterior doors

-	Fireplace

</airSeal>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.



</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>HEAT PUMPS- AIR SOURCE HEAT PUMP- ASHP AND CCASHP 

You are eligible to the heat pump grant from Energy Solution Centre, please consult their website for more information by following the link below:

https://yukon.ca/en/news/expanded-rebates-renewable-home-heating-now-available

ETS PROGRAM

For more information concerning the Electrical Thermal Storage Unit, please follow the link below:

http://yukonconservation.org/programs/energy/electric-thermal-storage#:~:text=Electric%20thermal%20storage%20(ETS)%20is,providing%20heat%20throughout%20the%20day 

</HeatingSystem>
                <Renewables>RENEWABLES

For any questions concerning the rebates and the programs about solar energy, please follow the link below to get more information:

https://yukon.ca/en/renewable-energy-rebate#eligible-renewable-systems





PLEASE NOTE: The photovoltaic suggested system, is based on the installation of 6 panels. This is only for suggestion purposes, the system might be composed of more than the suggested system.

</Renewables>
                <AdditionalComments>DEPRUSSIRAZION TEST

The depressurization test performed as shown a risk of combustion gas spillage. Therefore, we recommend verifying your carbon monoxide detectors regularly.





</AdditionalComments>
            </RURComments>
            <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="false" moistureProofCrawlSpace="false" waterproofing="false" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="false" sumpPump="false" smartThermostats="false" remoteCommunities="false" evaluationCost="">
                <Community>N/A</Community>
            </GreenerHomes>
        </Options>
